{"step_index":279,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T15:20:02Z","content":"CRITICAL INSTRUCTION 1: I will use `write_to_file` and `replace_file_content` concurrently to create the remaining MVC components (Controllers, Views).\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION 2: After the code is written, I will use `run_command` with `IsDaemon=true` to run the `.NET` application.","thinking":"**Defining the Scope**\n\nI've scoped the work needed. I now know I need to rewrite the Portal and Admin controllers and specific Razor views. I’m thinking about the interactions between the controllers and views to ensure smooth application execution. The goal is to successfully run the application.\n\n\n**Prioritizing the MVP**\n\nI've decided on the essential files for the MVP. I'll focus on `PortalController.cs`, `_Layout.cshtml`, `Index.cshtml`, and `HienTrang.cshtml`. I'll also add a seeding mechanism for instant data. Rather than a separate `DbInitializer`, I'll add the seeding right into `Program.cs` or `KtsDbContext` for now.\n\n\n**Defining the Actions**\n\nI'm now writing `PortalController.cs`, and the necessary views: `_ViewImports.cshtml`, `_ViewStart.cshtml`, `_Layout.cshtml`, `Index.cshtml`, and `HienTrang.cshtml`. I'll run the application in the background. The MVP scope has been further refined. I'll focus on the `PortalController` and associated views, using Tailwind CSS in `_Layout.cshtml`. I'll also add a `DbInitializer.cs` for dummy data to avoid an empty database. Then I'll run the app, and tell the user that the MVP (Portal) is running.\n\n\n**Implementing the Initializer**\n\nI've just implemented `DbInitializer.cs` and updated `Program.cs` to call it. I'm adding dummy data for \"Sở TT&TT\" and a system within it to ensure the app is no longer starting with an empty database, which is good. Now, I'm working on the `PortalController` and I'm ready to finally run the application with the initial data seed.\n\n\n**Constructing the Controller**\n\nI've just finished the `PortalController.cs` file, incorporating `Index` and `HienTrang` actions that will pull data from the database using Entity Framework Core. I'm working on the `HienTrang.cshtml` view now, with the goal of displaying the data in an organized way, most likely using an HTML table or cards. I'll test this out soon.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"using KtsVinhLong.Models;\nusing System.Linq;\n\nnamespace KtsVinhLong.Data\n{\n    public static class DbInitializer\n    {\n        public static void Initialize(KtsDbContext context)\n        {\n            context.Database.EnsureCreated();\n\n            if (context.HeThongSos.Any())\n            {\n                return; // Đã có dữ liệu\n            }\n\n            var donVi = new DonVi { Id = \"DV01\", Ten = \"Sở Thông tin và Truyền thông\", Loai = \"so\" };\n            context.DonVis.Add(donVi);\n\n            var heThongSos = new HeThongSo[]\n            {\n                new HeThongSo { Id = \"HT01\", Ma = \"HT-01\", Ten = \"Trục tích hợp chia sẻ dữ liệu LGSP\", Loai = \"du-lieu\", Lop = 2, ChuQuan = \"Sở TT&TT\", TrangThai = \"dang-van-hanh\", DonViId = \"DV01\" },\n                new HeThongSo { Id = \"HT02\", Ma = \"HT-02\", Ten = \"Hệ thống Quản lý Văn bản và Điều hành\", Loai = \"ung-dung\", Lop = 3, ChuQuan = \"Sở TT&TT\", TrangThai = \"dang-van-hanh\", DonViId = \"DV01\" },\n                new HeThongSo { Id = \"HT03\", Ma = \"HT-03\", Ten = \"Cổng Dịch vụ công trực tuyến\", Loai = \"kenh-tuong-tac\", Lop = 4, ChuQuan = \"Sở TT&TT\", TrangThai = \"dang-van-hanh\", DonViId = \"DV01\" },\n                new HeThongSo { Id = \"HT04\", Ma = \"HT-04\", Ten = \"Hệ thống Mạng diện rộng (WAN) tỉnh\", Loai = \"ha-tang\", Lop = 1, ChuQuan = \"Sở TT&TT\", TrangThai = \"dang-van-hanh\", DonViId = \"DV01\" }\n            };\n\n            context.HeThongSos.AddRange(heThongSos);\n            context.SaveChanges();\n        }\n    }\n}\n","Description":"Database Initializer to seed initial test data","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Delta Force\\KtsVinhLongNet\\KtsVinhLong\\Data\\DbInitializer.cs","toolAction":"Creating DbInitializer","toolSummary":"Create DbInitializer.cs"}}]}
